      "hints": [
        "Find $b = 16$ by setting $y = 0$.",
        "Integrate $4x^{1/2} - x$ to $\\frac{8}{3}x^{3/2} - \\frac{1}{2}x^2$.",
        "Evaluate between $x = 4$ and $x = 16$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the positive $x$-intercept $b$ by setting $y = 0$:\n$$4\\sqrt{x} - x = 0 \\implies \\sqrt{x}(4 - \\sqrt{x}) = 0 \\implies \\sqrt{x} = 4 \\implies b = 16$$",
        "Set up the definite integral for the area from $x = 4$ to $x = 16$:\n$$\\text{Area} = \\int_4^{16} (4x^{1/2} - x)\\,dx = \\left[\\frac{8}{3}x^{3/2} - \\frac{1}{2}x^2\\right]_4^{16}$$",
        "Evaluate at the upper limit $x = 16$:\n$$\\frac{8}{3}(16^{3/2}) - \\frac{1}{2}(16^2) = \\frac{8}{3}(64) - 128 = \\frac{512}{3} - 128 = \\frac{128}{3}$$",
        "Evaluate at the lower limit $x = 4$ and subtract:\n$$\\frac{8}{3}(4^{3/2}) - \\frac{1}{2}(4^2) = \\frac{8}{3}(8) - 8 = \\frac{64}{3} - 8 = \\frac{40}{3}$$\n$$\\text{Area} = \\frac{128}{3} - \\frac{40}{3} = \\frac{88}{3} = 29\\frac{1}{3}$$"
      ],
